 "$comment": "For scripts/web-scene-video.py: what may move in each illustrated scene, in fractions of the picture. nature: polygons (or boxes) where the clip may show at all, plus nature_dark in Dusk only; leafy: areas of which only the plant-coloured part counts (tree lines in front of buildings). Everything outside them, and everything in art/web/held/<scene>.png (the people and the objects), is the still picture in every frame; the drifting clouds are the only other thing that moves. hold / hold_dark: more that stays still; free: flowers that the held outlines caught by mistake. solo: things with a loop of their own (butterflies, birds); birds: fade over at the loop point instead of morphing."
